From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 18:29:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fire PlayerRespawnEvent, which this fork never fires

PlayerRespawnEvent is dead API here. Paper fires it from
ServerPlayer#findRespawnPositionAndUseSpawnBlock0, the single place that turns a
player's stored respawn data into the position they are about to be placed at.
Folia's ServerPlayer#respawn is a rewrite that resolves the position itself -
findRespawnAndUseSpawnBlock for a bed or anchor, fudgeSpawnLocation otherwise -
and hands it to placeInAsync, so that Paper method survives only as the
EndPortalBlock helper and the event is never constructed at all. Every plugin
that places a player after death is simply not called.

Fired at the head of the waiter Folia attaches to its spawnPosComplete, which is
the instant the position is final and before anything is applied. Not adopted
because it was the obvious spot - checked, because three separate properties had
to hold there:

  - Both resolution paths end at that one completion, so a single hook covers
    bed, respawn anchor, missing respawn block and plain world spawn.
  - CallbackCompletable runs its waiters on the completing thread, and both paths
    complete out of a chunk-load callback. ChunkTaskScheduler#scheduleChunkLoad
    re-dispatches to the region that owns the chunk when the caller does not own
    it, so the completing thread always owns the respawn position. That is a
    tick thread, and it is the one the anchor write below needs.
  - The waiter already reads its destination world back out of the location it is
    given and hands it to placeInAsync, which queues onto the destination
    region's own task queue - so a handler moving the player to another world
    needs no extra plumbing.

isBedSpawn and isAnchorSpawn are taken from the RespawnPosAngle the platform just
resolved rather than from a second block read, so the event reports what the
respawn actually used. isMissingRespawnBlock is set on the branch where a stored
respawn config resolved to no spawn position, which is the branch Paper reports
through TeleportTransition.missingRespawnBlock.

Respawn anchors: Paper consumes the charge after the event and only when a
handler did not move the player (SPIGOT-5989). Folia builds the same
consumeAnchorCharge runnable inside findRespawnAndUseSpawnBlock and never runs
it, so on stock an anchor is never depleted even though the depletion sound
plays. Restoring the event restores the rule that governs it, on the thread that
owns the anchor.

One bounded difference, stated rather than hidden: Paper aborts the respawn if
the player disconnected while handlers ran. It can, because at that point they
have not been removed from the world. Here they have - respawn calls
removePlayerImmediately before the position is resolved - so refusing to place
them would strand the entity outside every world. The placement always
completes and a player who left is cleaned up by the normal disconnect path.

Kill switch: event-config.respawn-event=false.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
index 28ce624e9952e9d45930d4550ef80d1e788f5916..db7e811d5b133557025f117ff9fabf0e9c670ad2 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerPlayer.java
@@ -1810,9 +1810,28 @@ public class ServerPlayer extends Player implements ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patc
         ca.spottedleaf.concurrentutil.completable.CallbackCompletable<org.bukkit.Location> spawnPosComplete =
             new ca.spottedleaf.concurrentutil.completable.CallbackCompletable<>();
         boolean[] usedRespawnAnchor = new boolean[1];
+        // Lecithin start - fire PlayerRespawnEvent
+        // The three flags Paper hands the event, filled in by whichever resolution path runs:
+        // [0] bed spawn, [1] respawn-anchor spawn, [2] the respawn block is gone. All false is the
+        // plain world-spawn case, which is what Paper's TeleportTransition.createDefault reports.
+        final boolean[] lecithinRespawnFlags = new boolean[3];
+        // Paper's own charge-consumption runnable, run only if the event leaves the location alone.
+        final Runnable[] lecithinConsumeAnchorCharge = new Runnable[1];
+        // Lecithin end
 
         // set up post spawn location logic
         spawnPosComplete.addWaiter((spawnLoc, throwable) -> {
+            // Lecithin start - fire PlayerRespawnEvent, which this platform never fires at all.
+            // Here because this is the instant the position is final and nothing has been applied
+            // yet, and because CallbackCompletable runs its waiters on the completing thread - a
+            // chunk-load callback on the region that owns the respawn position. See
+            // LecithinRespawnEvents for why that thread is the one the anchor write needs.
+            spawnLoc = fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinRespawnEvents.callRespawnEvent(
+                ServerPlayer.this, spawnLoc, reason,
+                lecithinRespawnFlags[0], lecithinRespawnFlags[1], lecithinRespawnFlags[2],
+                lecithinConsumeAnchorCharge[0]
+            );
+            // Lecithin end
             // update pos and velocity
             ServerPlayer.this.setPosRaw(spawnLoc.getX(), spawnLoc.getY(), spawnLoc.getZ());
             ServerPlayer.this.setYRot(spawnLoc.getYaw());
@@ -1869,6 +1888,7 @@ public class ServerPlayer extends Player implements ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patc
                     ).orElse(null);
                     if (spawnPos == null) {
                         // no spawn
+                        lecithinRespawnFlags[2] = true; // Lecithin - PlayerRespawnEvent#isMissingRespawnBlock
                         ServerPlayer.this.connection.send(
                             new ClientboundGameEventPacket(ClientboundGameEventPacket.NO_RESPAWN_BLOCK_AVAILABLE, 0.0F)
                         );
@@ -1883,6 +1903,14 @@ public class ServerPlayer extends Player implements ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patc
                     boolean isRespawnAnchor = respawnWorld.getBlockState(respawnConfig.respawnData.pos()).is(net.minecraft.world.level.block.Blocks.RESPAWN_ANCHOR);
                     boolean isBed = respawnWorld.getBlockState(respawnConfig.respawnData.pos()).is(net.minecraft.tags.BlockTags.BEDS);
                     usedRespawnAnchor[0] = !alive && isRespawnAnchor;
+                    // Lecithin start - PlayerRespawnEvent#isBedSpawn/#isAnchorSpawn and SPIGOT-5989.
+                    // Taken from the RespawnPosAngle the platform just resolved rather than from a
+                    // second block read, so the event reports what the respawn actually used. The
+                    // charge runnable is the platform's own; stock builds it here and never runs it.
+                    lecithinRespawnFlags[0] = spawnPos.isBedSpawn();
+                    lecithinRespawnFlags[1] = spawnPos.isAnchorSpawn();
+                    lecithinConsumeAnchorCharge[0] = spawnPos.consumeAnchorCharge();
+                    // Lecithin end
 
                     // finished now, pass the location on
                     spawnPosComplete.complete(
